<speak>
<s>This is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">29072026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="95%">
<s>Saudi jets have struck Iraqi soil for the first time in this war, flying alongside American aircraft against Iran-aligned logistics sites, after what <sub alias="Central Command">CENTCOM</sub> counts as more than thirty drone attacks in seventy-two hours.</s> <s>Riyadh spent a decade avoiding open kinetic participation in a confrontation between Washington and Tehran, and a single sortie has ended that posture — over a third country, Iraq, whose government says it wasn't consulted.</s> <s>Baghdad now has to explain to its own parliament why two foreign air forces operate over its provinces... and it hasn't yet.</s>
</prosody>
<p>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Leaked cables published by Drop Site News show a Saudi Special Committee was instructed in twenty-twelve to engineer a rift inside Yemen's Zaydi community and target Ansarallah — three years before the war began.</s> <s>The standard account has the kingdom reacting in twenty-fifteen to a Houthi takeover, and the committee sat outside the ordinary ministries, which is how a state runs a war file without leaving a public record in the institutions that would keep one.</s> <s>Riyadh hasn't responded to the leak, and the full authentication of the documents remains open.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>At least thirty-two protesters have been killed in Rawalakot in two days, and Pakistan's defence minister Khawaja Asif is reported to have called Azad Kashmir's demonstrators enemies like India.</s> <s>That's the fourth step in a week — concession, proscription, the religious anathema of branding them khawarij, and now placement outside the nation altogether — and each step widens the legal category under which force may be used.</s> <s>Kashmiris there elect an assembly with no seats in Pakistan's parliament, so a grievance over flour and electricity tariffs has no ordinary political route... which is how it reaches the street, and then the mortuary.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Honduras's former president Juan Orlando Hernández, convicted in a New York court of running his country's institutions for cocaine traffickers and sentenced to forty-five years, is home and free by American presidential pardon.</s> <s>Clemency erases the sentence without touching a single finding of fact, so the conviction stands as a record while the punishment evaporates, and no prosecutor may appeal it.</s> <s>Defence lawyers from Tegucigalpa to Quito now have a precedent that a sentence is negotiable somewhere above the court that imposed it.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>In Kumamoto, rescuers are still pulling survivors from a collapsed shopping mall as Japan's earthquake toll reaches thirteen, with two hundred and sixty thousand people told to evacuate.</s> <s>The collapse is the anomaly: Japan's post-nineteen-eighty-one seismic code is the strictest on earth, and large commercial structures aren't supposed to pancake at this magnitude, so what matters is when that building was last retrofitted.</s> <s>Survival under rubble falls away sharply after seventy-two hours, which is why Prime Minister Takaichi is calling it a race — and why the first day decides the final number more than the magnitude does.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Sudan's army has retaken Bara, and General el-Burhan flew in by helicopter to stand in it.</s> <s>Bara sits on the road from Omdurman to El Obeid, which is the corridor deciding whether a besieged city of hundreds of thousands can be resupplied by land rather than by negotiation with the men encircling it.</s> <s>A Rapid Support Forces source disputes any decisive victory, saying it still holds the water sources ringing El Obeid — and in a siege, water outranks a road.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>The <sub alias="United Nations">UN</sub> human rights chief Volker Türk says violations recorded in Lebanon may amount to war crimes, with a thousand people now sheltering in a single repurposed school in Beirut.</s> <s>A finding is not a prosecution — only the Human Rights Council or a referral to the International Criminal Court carries consequence, and Lebanon isn't a party to the Rome Statute, so it cannot refer Israel itself.</s> <s>That leaves the record complete and the route to a courtroom closed.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>In Gaza, cash converters are charging commissions of up to fifty percent, because the siege has forced an economy onto e-wallets it has no power to run.</s> <s>Paper money works in a blackout; a digital transfer needs electricity, a tower, a server and a solvent bank, and the Palestine Monetary Authority says strikes have kept it from reopening branches or supplying new notes.</s> <s>So the poorest households pay a tax to touch their own money — levied by nobody in particular, and collected all the same.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Iran's Revolutionary Guard says it disabled three tankers in the Strait of Hormuz for taking what it called an unauthorised passage, and Brent rebounded three point two percent to eighty-six dollars and eighty cents.</s> <s>That phrase is the whole story: the law of the sea grants transit passage a coastal state may not suspend, and firing on a vessel for using the wrong lane turns a shipping scheme into a checkpoint.</s> <s>The cost travels through war-risk insurance rather than crude — premiums reprice within days, and they're paid by importers in Karachi and Dhaka, not by Tehran or Washington.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Whoosh, Indonesia's high-speed line from Jakarta to Bandung and the first in Southeast Asia, is still losing money.</s> <s>Built on Chinese loans, it's the flagship of a decade of infrastructure diplomacy in which the engineering has consistently arrived on time and the passenger forecasts consistently haven't.</s> <s>Analysts are now asking the question no launch ceremony covers — whether the losses become a permanent claim on Indonesia's public finances.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Russia's central bank has published draft rules for a domestic crypto depository, days after fresh European sanctions on Russian-linked crypto firms.</s> <s>A depository is simply the registry of who owns what, and a domestic one lets Moscow settle ownership without any foreign custodian that sanctions can reach.</s> <s>Sanctions work through intermediaries — and this is a state methodically building the intermediaries it controls.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Researchers warn that mosquito populations are activating detoxifying enzymes against a widely used insecticide far faster than control programmes can respond.</s> <s>This is metabolic resistance — cytochrome enzymes that dismantle the compound before it ever reaches the nervous system — and unlike the slow resistance public health has managed for decades, one enzyme family can degrade several unrelated chemicals, so populations arrive already resistant to compounds they've never met.</s> <s>Bed nets and indoor spraying across sub-Saharan Africa and South Asia rest entirely on that chemistry, and replacements are procured in years, not generations.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>In Seoul, researchers have released one thousand and eighty gene-expression profiles mapping what traditional herbal prescriptions actually do inside human cells.</s> <s>Four cell lines from lung, liver, colon and brain were dosed with extracts to build the resource, an attempt to take remedies used by hundreds of millions and put a measurable mechanism under them.</s> <s>It's published as a provisional manuscript... and the harder question of which effects survive in a body remains untouched.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A Bayesian reconstruction of Portugal's twenty-twenty epidemic finds adults, not children, drove the country's first wave.</s> <s>The authors modelled two counterfactuals — schools staying open that spring, and closing again that autumn — and conclude closures alone rarely stop a wave.</s> <s>Millions of children lost a year of schooling on the opposite assumption, and the accounting for that has barely begun.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Tata and Mahindra have come first in a global battery-efficiency ranking from the International Council on Clean Transportation, ahead of both Tesla and <sub alias="B Y D">BYD</sub> on kilometres per kilowatt-hour.</s> <s>They trail on range and charging speed, which is the trade being made deliberately: efficiency means a smaller battery, less lithium, and a lower price.</s> <s>That's the variable that decides whether electric cars reach Indian and African households, rather than the ones that decide magazine reviews.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>In Casa Grande, Arizona, a resident named Jacob Petrosky stood before his city council and proposed, in detail, a system to track the movements of council members — then revealed the pitch was satire, mirroring the licence-plate network they were about to approve for everyone else.</s> <s>Flock cameras read and store every plate that passes, and the data pools into a national searchable network shared across thousands of agencies, so a municipal purchase enrols residents in a system nobody in that room audits or can delete from.</s> <s>The same vendors are selling the same architecture as smart-city packages across the Gulf, Turkey and Southeast Asia, and the question of who queries the database is almost never asked at the point of sale.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Xbox was down for fifteen hours, and players who owned their games on physical discs were locked out along with everyone else.</s> <s>A shared internal Microsoft licensing service failed, and discs require an entitlement check before they'll run, so the plastic in the tray turned out to be a receipt rather than a copy.</s> <s>The new chief technology officer has promised a review of why one service could do that — the more useful question being what else you own that quietly needs permission.</s>
</p>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="90%">
<s>That's your briefing.</s>
</prosody>
</speak>